courses.learning_outcomes:
After completing this course, students should be able to:
(CLO 1) appreciate the significance of business ethics and corporate social responsibility in contemporary business environment;
(CLO 2) understand the principles of business entrepreneurship and its significance in the business economy in Hong Kong and the Mainland;
(CLO 3) compile a business plan to start up a business (or enhance existing business) providing innovative yet feasible business solutions;
(CLO 4) demonstrate effective oral and written communication skills in presenting business problems and solutions.

After completing this course, students should be able to:

(CLO 1) understand the financial reporting requirements of business combinations and group reporting under the international accounting context and the Hong Kong accounting reporting environment;
(CLO 2) compile group financial statements in accordance with relevant accounting standards;
(CLO 3) apply accounting and financial reporting knowledge, such as group reporting issues, in business decision-making;
(CLO 4) understand business and accounting issues from a global perspective, such as entities with overseas operations; and
(CLO 5) demonstrate effective written communication skills.

